To find the percentage of the river's total water used by Colorado City for non-industrial purposes, multiply 40% by 80%:
\begin{align*}
40\% \times 80\% &= \frac{40}{100} \times \frac{80}{100} \\
&= \frac{40 \times 80}{100 \times 100} \\
&= \frac{3200}{10000} \\
&= \boxed{32\%}
\end{align*}
